OL,3,GWest Midlands
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FA bright and cold start. Then,
OL,6,Fa very sunny, dry day. It will be
OL,7,Fchilly with a gentle northerly breeze
OL,8,Fand temperatures remaining a few
OL,9,Fdegrees below the seasonal average.
OL,10,
OL,11,CTonight:FA dry night ahead with plenty
OL,12,Fof clear spells. Temperatures will
OL,13,Ffall sharply overnight beneath long
OL,14,Fclear spells as winds ease and a
OL,15,Fwidespread frost is likely.
OL,16,
OL,17,CThursday:FA cold start, but dry and
OL,18,Fsunny throughout the day. Another
OL,19,Fchilly day, with temperatures a few
OL,20,Fdegrees below average for the time of
OL,21,Fyear, but only a light breeze.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
